# Executor-owed, BOX-LOCAL artefacts. ⛔ Never committed: PINNED_SRC_REV is the
# pin THIS BOX made after ITS bundle sync, and SRC_CLEAN.jsonl / SELFTEST_*.json
# / SMOKE_*.json / IDENT_*.json are that box's own launch ledger. A committed
# pin would let one box's rev masquerade as the other's — the exact IS-A1
# confusion `cross_box_rev_gate` exists to refuse.
#
# ⚠️ THE GOLDEN GATE IS **NOT** IN THIS DIRECTORY AT ALL. This round INHERITS
# `../fpu_ladder_prep/FPU_BITEXACT_LADDER.json` (itself gitignored and BOX-LOCAL,
# because `carc_rs_binary_sha` differs between boxes compiling identical source)
# and `run_cells.sh` re-asserts its wheel against this box's installed binary.
# DESIGN §9 states the inheritance argument and names the two gaps the --smoke
# IDENT legs pay.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ EVERY PATTERN IS ANCHORED WITH A LEADING `/`. An unanchored
# `PINNED_SRC_REV` matches at ANY DEPTH and therefore swallows
# `selftest_fixture/PINNED_SRC_REV` — which is a COMMITTED FIXTURE FILE (the
# synthetic 40-hex pin `aaaa…` that `analyze_h2h.py --selftest` reads to
# exercise `cross_box_rev_gate`). Without the anchor the selftest raises on a
# fresh clone, which would make the launcher's precondition ladder fail on every
# box that had not run make_fixture.py first. (Inherited verbatim from
# fpu_ladder_prep, where it was learned the hard way.)
/PINNED_SRC_REV
/SRC_CLEAN.jsonl
/SELFTEST_*.json
/SMOKE_*.json
/IDENT_*.json
# ⛔ `H2H_VERDICT.json` is NOT here on purpose: the READ-OUT is the round's
# deliverable and is COMMITTED, exactly as fpu_ladder_prep/LADDER_VERDICT.json is.
/BAND_CLAIMED
/logs/
/__pycache__/
/selftest_fixture/__pycache__/
